From 6eb0bc15a5a91bd1131896d767e8f4de7641811a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aravind <aravindsprint@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:20:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Per-user scoping: every API returns only the GST User's
 businesses

New litwatch/scope.py decides which Businesses a request may see:
- the logged-in user's GST User, or for System Manager / the shared API key the
  GST User passed as gstUser (query, form or JSON) or X-LitWatch-GST-User header
- System Manager users without a GST User record, and unscoped staff calls, see
  everything; any other user without a GST User record gets 404 (as get_clients did)

Applied through:
- permission_query_conditions for Business, GSTIN, Notice, Payment, Review Queue
  Item, Client Document, Audit Log, GST User, GST Sync Log, GST OTP Request
  (filters every list and the Resource API, also for Administrator)
- has_permission in those controllers (single-record read/update/delete/create,
  which a hook alone can't do for Administrator)
- the custom methods: get_clients, get_businesses, get_client_pipeline,
  set_active_client, get_active_client, update_client_pipeline_stage, add_gstin,
  get_gstin_connections, connect/verify/resend/sync, run_all_gstin_sync,
  get_sync_log, get_sync_usage, get_client_notices, get_command_hub,
  get_gstin_gsp_details
- a Business created by a scoped user is added to their GST User

Tests: litwatch/tests/test_user_scoping.py

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016uSTwic31grtwzMMK7rPAR
